Third-party code in tools/ (incident I-199, tools/thermal.mjs: the iPhone's thermal condition)

The files below port or follow code from the projects listed here. Each file's header names its sources. This repo
stays local (CLAUDE.md Hard rule 2); this notice keeps the licences' attribution terms all the same.
pymobiledevice3 (GPL-3.0) was read for understanding only; no code was copied from it.


1. appium-ios, https://github.com/appium/appium-ios, commit bd9ba5fd86b87035b15023ae46d3bcec928266b5
   Licence: Apache License, Version 2.0. Copyright JS Foundation and other contributors, https://js.foundation
   The full licence text: http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
   Changes: rewritten in plain ES modules with no dependencies and reduced to what thermal.mjs uses; NSError kept
   as an object; the phone's DTX aux header is accepted with any buffer-size field; RSD reached through the address
   of macOS's own CoreDevice tunnel (netstat + lsof) and not through appium's tunnel registry.

